--- body ---
## Context
Routing moves from the deterministic model-level x effort chooser to the
orchestrating LLM choosing from the grid (tracker 1052). Haiku 5.5 is absent
from `skills/route/grid.json` and `routes.json`; its arm-N data sits in
`docs/tournament-graphs/haiku55-results.csv`. SpaceBunny is dead and removed
at the author's request.

`scripts/tournament-analysis.py` only refreshes numeric fields of EXISTING
grid rows keyed by `row["arm"]`; arm discovery reads `~/arena/runs.json`
`arm_order` (no `n`), so a hand-added `"arm": "n"` row would raise `KeyError`.
Line ~190 hardcodes `failures=0/30` in the quality string.

## Scope
- Extend arm discovery to include arm `n` (or add it to `arm_order`), add a
  lineage `family` emitter (Anthropic, OpenAI, Mistral, Qwen, DeepSeek, GLM;
  independent of provider or door), add the Haiku 5.5 row, run `--grid`.
- Fix the hardcoded `failures=0/30`; point the grid `_comment` numeric source
  at the Haiku data (the corrected-summary JSON has none).
- Add Haiku 5.5 to the Anthropic entry of `routes.json`; note that its price
  multiplies by 5 above 100k prompt tokens.
- Remove SpaceBunny: the `routes.json` entry, the grid-comment wording (via
  the generator), the example at `skills/route/SKILL.md:110`. Leave the
  historical docs.
- Check the `~/arena/runs/*-n` legs have complete judge files so Haiku is
  marked final, not provisional.

## Exit criteria
- [x] `grid.json` and `routes.json` parse; the grid shows Haiku 5.5 and a `family` per identity
- [x] `grep -ri spacebunny skills/` finds nothing
- [x] Haiku 5.5 is marked final, or the reason it is provisional is recorded
- [x] `make check` passes
